  "changes": [
    {
      "id": "weekly-upstream-20261101",
      "notes": "Portable reasoning maps against model-supported effort sets while provider reasoningEffort remains unchanged; GPT-5.6 Chat function tools disable portable reasoning and GPT-6.1 Terra supports non-reasoning sampling. GPT-5 keeps cache retention and Responses logprobs. Untyped propertyNames constraints are removed with one warning; completion errors contain misplaced system content. Searching web-search terminals are errors through the shared generation/stream/batch parser. Decisions sends bounded object/object-array evidence as input_json and promptCacheKey, with UTF-8/depth/value limits and text fallback. REST transcription uses catalog-equivalent defaults only for Whisper/diarization, timestamps only with verbose_json and duration-billed usage fallback. Native streaming transcription adds the published realtime-whisper/Live/turn-based models and dated aliases, languages/delay policy, raw deltas/final events and cancellation. Native async API key suppliers resolve per authenticated HTTP request and server WebSocket connection; explicit provider/request auth headers retain precedence. Files managed operations and streaming multipart resolve before send; Skills and Batch use the shared credential-aware transport. Reviewed upstream: @ai-sdk/openai 4.0.102 to 4.0.106. Validation passed: node Scripts/test-packages.mjs (all 52 owning package suites and the compatibility facade); node Scripts/sdk.mjs generate --check; node --test Scripts/tests/*.test.cjs (27 passed); docs-site check and build (100 pages). Live provider calls were not run.",
      "compatibility": "Minor release for additive native API; existing static settings and call sites remain compatible. Updated direct dependency minimums are recorded in the manifest. Existing documented JS/framework and native product gaps remain; version-delta review does not imply full parity or live-service testing. Explicit custom authentication skips an unused credential supplier, a deliberate native callback-order adaptation."
    }
  ],
